# link_pack -- packer -> unpacker round trip: same words, order and fields; flit parity and size; CRC flush; progress
# BW = 16, WPF = 32, XW = YW = 3 (the silicon links), the drop 0.41 packer with its registered link side: the beats out
# carry the words accepted, in order, none invented or repeated, with their type / tag / head / stream fields and PSUM
# columns; every link flit even parity and 1..WPF words, every beat out even parity and 1..BW words; a CRC (any one-word
# type) accepted leaves only itself in flight; with the sink ready no beat waits more than 2 cycles (the bound of the
# combinational link side: the register did not add a cycle). Full proof by k-induction with invariants over the output
# register, the pending flit and a ghost of its prefix word parities (drop 0.41); link_pack_fv.sv holds the harness.
# The engine is bitwuzla: the running parity's induction step (word parities through the merge's barrel shift) does not
# close with yices in 540 s, bitwuzla closes the whole set in about two minutes.
[options]
mode prove
depth 2

[engines]
smtbmc bitwuzla

[script]
plugin -i slang
read_slang -DFORMAL --top link_pack_fv link_pack.sv link_pack_fv.sv
prep -top link_pack_fv

[files]
rtl/link_pack.sv
formal/link_pack_fv.sv
